From d1a73d0355eeb3e689d7d3331fb41fc28daebfa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Gehann <fg@fgehann.de>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:18:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] dnf5: Report item progress, speed and size left

Package downloads only reported an overall percentage, so clients could
not show which package is being downloaded, how fast, or how much is
left. Report each package as downloading when its download starts, with
its own item progress, and report the download speed and the remaining
download size of the job.

Transactions that do not download anything, like removals, no longer
claim to be downloading.

The download callbacks are only installed on the base while
downloading, as the base outlives the job they report to.

Add unit tests for the dnf5 backend, covering the download progress.

Part of: https://github.com/PackageKit/PackageKit/issues/1019
