From 493bcbd0ed9cc2b8d1666d7432927b52c90f756a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Gehann <fg@fgehann.de>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:15:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] dnf5: Weigh install progress by package size

The percentage of a transaction counted the processed packages, so the
small packages that are usually installed first moved it most of the
way before the large ones, which take most of the time, even started.
Installing seven packages of 136 MiB showed 57% in the first 100 ms.

Let the packages being installed split their share of the percentage
by their installed size, as writing their files takes most of the
time. Removing a package takes about as long whatever its size, so
removed packages, also the old versions of updated ones, keep an equal
share each, as before.

Related: https://github.com/PackageKit/PackageKit/issues/1019
---
 backends/dnf5/dnf5-backend-thread.cpp |   5 +-
 backends/dnf5/dnf5-backend-utils.cpp  | 112 ++++++++++++++------
