From 13d22896c607caaa4119ad726914736992c139c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Gehann <fg@fgehann.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:57:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] dnf5: Complete transaction item and removal progress

DNF5 only reported per-package download progress, leaving installed and
removed items unfinished. RPM can also omit its final progress callback,
leaving a successful removal below 100%.

Report item progress and Finished notifications with the original
package ID. Complete the weighted share at the element stop callback,
including unknown totals, and set successful transaction progress to
100% after reloading the repositories.

Add regression tests for partial callbacks, item completion and removals
without progress callbacks. All five PackageKit suites and real patched
Discover scenarios pass on this branch.

Use the existing 1.4.x package notification API. Eight checks with
unmodified pkcon 1.4.0 and its API 18 library pass; public API and D-Bus
definitions remain unchanged.
